# Inert private scope/source facts (SOURCE/PURE ONLY)

The fixed API takes actor, keys and exact registered worklist, NOT an older permission receipt. It first revalidates the complete relevant closure and scalar candidate inventories, then calls fixed compose_permissions and consumes its one-use receipt immediately, then computes scope/source facts. No caller callback or writes intervene. A previously composed worklist is rejected, not revived using inventory equality. Native reader grants/private inputs are evaluated by that fresh composition; inventory equality alone is NOT proof of current permission after same-connection grant/payload changes.

Original native-filter exclusions (all relevant historical claimed templates minus candidates) are unioned with authentic freshly denied candidate templates. Hidden scopes use ALL historical claims to those same-case hidden templates: no retraction/active/owner-current/resolution-winner shortcut. The native finance document_type exclusion is separate and applies to empty finance_report/finance_group_report scopes without claims. Ordinary empty scopes do not gain an invented denial.

Exact four hidden-scope source relations are retained: scope.evidence, claim.evidence→scope, resolution.evidence→scope, retraction.evidence→claim.scope. Shared linked scopes are classified internally, not automatically treated as selected scopes. Source eligibility is the native explicit template_current_source OR policy_decision/public_evidence condition; public_evidence is called UNCHANGED, not reconstructed or narrowed to same-case forecast internals. No Evidence.body or private payload is transferred. Explicit source kind is not accidentally vetoed by generic PRIVATE.

IMPORTANT resource contract: returned scalar rows and callsite attempts are bounded; native public_evidence contains global forecast JSON array expansion/bigint casts. This stage does NOT bound that inner database work, SQL CPU, planner memory or runtime. One charged query is not a global-work bound. Native query errors remain fatal; no public fallback, JSON containment rewrite or new row guards. No query was executed for these source checks.

The same entry-owned scalar closure/worklist counters charge fixed queries/gates and relevant IDs; each result has limit+1 admission. Scope/evidence/template sets stay100 and existing aggregate/phase caps remain unchanged. Historical repeated claims use DISTINCT scope IDs/EXISTS semantics, not an expanded Python edge graph or unrelated-history cap. Complete closure/candidate Finance/PMO tuple inventories are rechecked before return; the scope/source outcome is also recomputed and compared under the fixed read-only path, including finance-read status. Changed topology/filter/inventory or facts, overflow, context/query/permission errors poison the entry and return no partial facts. RR does not itself protect own writes; this is a trusted fixed read-only sequence, not a hostile-writer sandbox or universal grant/currentness proof.

Facts are frozen, repr-suppressed, exact-object registered under the original witness/worklist/fresh consumed receipt and can be privately consumed once. Stage registry is bounded100 and same worklist cannot reset/retry after completion or failure. Old/copy facts misuse poisons original/current entries. Facts contain private hidden-scope and eligible-source sets, not public IDs or metadata output. Consumption is not new authorization after arbitrary later writes. No owner metadata adapter, route, status/selection, user-facing visibility or source-body access is activated. Future adapters must prove their exact native require_scope/visible_sources needs; selected record evidence is not assumed automatically subject to both gates.

14 new pure definitions plus154 prior composed checks pass normal/-O (168 total). Tests exercise actual fresh composition/receipt with fixed reader stand-ins, older-receipt rejection, inventory/final fact mutations, fatal native predicate error, copied/old facts, filtered+denied templates, historical/retracted claims, empty finance/ordinary scopes, four distinct links, explicit source-kind OR and policy public requirement, foreign IDs and overflow. The public-evidence stand-in tests only the preserved call contract, NOT the native global JSON/cast semantics. No actual SQL, native permissions, constructors, providers, held code, fixtures or runtime proof. DB-forbidden static/model/exact14 existing native discovery remains source-only; native tests UNRUN.

Remaining: full native/default-prepared and adapter equivalence, permitted actual fixtures and storage-cleared SQL/concurrency/rollback validation, outer selected-owner admission limits, and any separately requested true inner-work bound. None is an invented HOD policy decision or a full milestone claim.
